From 3553b8cc294f547386d9cb47d8e1976da981d637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:39:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Autorun fixes: endless turn, turn time, settler delivery,
 garrison and gold

Found by loading the reported save (Marathon, 410 BC) into the real DLL in a
headless harness and letting every player play on.

- Endless turn: groupPathTo ends a mission whose next step no unit can take as
  a move; groupMove split the lone unit into a new group on every update
  slice. Worker jobs skip plots with visible enemies; a per-turn watchdog ends
  the moves of a unit that keeps losing its group.
- Turn time (9.6 s -> 2.6 s per turn on the save): pathValid keeps its
  parent-plot answer while the A* expands that plot; AI_explore searches
  candidates best bound first; AI_exploreRange skips plots out of range by a
  path-turn lower bound; upgrade reachability is computed once; canTradeItem
  tests validity before denial; Himeji lookup in the gold callbacks.
- Settlers: land and sea delivery regions from our cities and ports; only
  deliverable sites count for production and are searched; settlers without
  any deliverable site are disbanded after a grace period; lone settlers take
  a spare defender; a transport without escort returns to port; cities build
  a transport for a waiting settler whose sites need one.
- Garrison: a city that cannot train a city-defence unit counts all its land
  defenders (endless Spearmen otherwise).
- Gold target: elapsed turns at the standard speed's pace and a calendar-based
  liquidity cap; Marathon AIs no longer bank gold at 5-25% research.

New tests: test_turn_end_guard, test_settle_reach, test_gold_target_speed.
See Docs/MASINISSA_AUTORUN_FIXES.md.
